      {
       "type": "text",
       "text": "I haven't entered this order yet. I need you to confirm the dose first.\n\n**Amlodipine 50 mg is 5 times the maximum recommended adult dose.** The usual adult range is 2.5\u201310 mg by mouth once daily, and 10 mg/day is the maximum. A 50 mg dose could cause severe low blood pressure, reflex tachycardia, and shock. Calcium channel blocker overdoses are hard to reverse, and amlodipine's long half-life (30\u201350 hours) means the effects can last for days.\n\nThis looks like a possible typo for **5 mg**, which is a common starting dose.\n\nPlease confirm which you want:\n1. **Amlodipine 5 mg PO once daily**, if 50 mg was a typo\n2. **Another dose** within the 2.5\u201310 mg range\n3. **50 mg as written**, if this is intentional. If so, please give the clinical reason so I can record it on the order. A dose this high would usually also need pharmacy review.\n\nOnce you confirm, I'll enter the order."
      }
     ],
